---
permalink: "/terms/"
pageTitle: "Terms of Sale"
pageDescription: "The terms that apply when you buy printed mental health sheets from Kelly Marie Wellbeing."
eleventyComputed:
  # Kept out of search engines, and out of the footer, until a pack is on sale.
  noindex: "{{ '' if shopPage.selling else 'yes' }}"
---
{#- Terms for sheets bought through the Shop page's Stripe links. Not in the CMS (like the
    privacy policy); the business address comes from "Page: Shop". Linked from the footer
    and under the Buy buttons once any pack is on sale (shopPage.selling). -#}
{%- set orgName = content.header.logoLine1 + " " + content.header.logoLine2 -%}
{% include "site-header.njk" %}

<section class="bg-stone py-20">
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 text-center">
    <h1 class="font-serif text-forest text-4xl lg:text-5xl leading-tight">Terms of Sale</h1>
    <div class="divider mt-6 mb-6 mx-auto"></div>
    <p class="text-gray-600">Last updated: October 2026</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="bg-white py-16">
  <div class="privacy max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">

    <p>
      These terms apply when you buy printed sheets from our <a href="/shop/">shop</a>. Please read them before you
      buy. If you're buying as a consumer, nothing in them affects your legal rights.
    </p>

    <h2>Who we are</h2>
    <p>
      {{ orgName }} is a partnership run by Kelly Marie and Ella Kitching.
    </p>
    <p>
      Address: {% if shopPage.address %}{{ shopPage.address }}{% else %}<strong>[business address to be added]</strong>{% endif %}<br />
      Email: <a href="mailto:{{ content.contact.email }}">{{ content.contact.email }}</a>
    </p>

    <h2>Ordering and payment</h2>
    <p>
      You order and pay on a secure checkout page run by Stripe, our payment provider. We never see or store your
      card details. The price shown on our shop is the price you pay, and UK delivery is free. Your order is
      accepted when your payment goes through and you receive a confirmation email.
    </p>

    <h2>Your support contacts</h2>
    <p>
      Every pack can include your own support contacts, printed on each {{ shopPage.series.quickTips or "Quick Tips" }} sheet. You give them at
      checkout, and we print them exactly as you give them, so please check them carefully. If anything looks wrong or won't fit, we'll email you before printing.
      Only include people's names and numbers if they've agreed to be listed.
    </p>

    <h2>Delivery</h2>
    <p>
      We post orders free of charge to the UK address you give at checkout, usually within 5 working days of
      payment. If there's a delay, we'll tell you. If we haven't sent your order within 30 days, you can cancel for
      a full refund.
    </p>

    <h2>Cancelling and returns</h2>
    <p>
      If you're buying as a consumer, the law usually lets you cancel within 14 days of receiving an order.
    </p>
    <p>
      Because every pack is printed with your own support contacts, it's made specially for you, so this right to
      cancel doesn't apply once we've started printing. Before then, email us and we'll cancel and refund your order
      in full. After that, packs can't be returned unless they're faulty or we've made a mistake.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you leave the support contacts blank, your pack isn't personalised, so you can cancel within 14 days of
      receiving it. Email us, then post the sheets back unused within 14 days; return postage is your cost. We'll
      refund you within 14 days of getting them back.
    </p>
    <p>
      The legal right to cancel is for consumers. If you're buying for your organisation and need to change an order,
      email us and we'll do our best to help.
    </p>

    <h2>Faulty or damaged sheets</h2>
    <p>
      If your sheets arrive damaged, misprinted or not as described, email us, ideally with a photo, and we'll
      replace them or give you a refund.
    </p>

    <h2>About the content</h2>
    <p>
      The sheets give general information about mental health. They aren't medical advice, a diagnosis or a
      replacement for professional support. Anyone who is struggling should speak to their GP or a qualified
      professional. In an emergency, call 999.
    </p>
    <p>
      The sheets are our copyright. Please don't copy, scan or reproduce them, in print or online, without our
      permission.
    </p>

    <h2>Our responsibility to you</h2>
    <p>
      We're responsible for losses you suffer that are a foreseeable result of us breaking these terms. We're not
      responsible for losses that weren't foreseeable, or for business losses such as lost profit. Nothing here limits
      our responsibility where the law doesn't allow it to be limited.
    </p>

    <h2>Your information</h2>
    <p>
      How we use the details you give when you order is explained in our <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>The law</h2>
    <p>
      These terms are governed by UK law. If you're a consumer, you can bring a claim in the courts of the part of the
      UK where you live. If there's a problem, please email us first and we'll try to put it right.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
    <p>We may update these terms from time to time. The terms in place when you placed your order apply to it.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .privacy > * + * { margin-top: 1rem; }
  .privacy h2 { font-family: 'Playfair Display', Georgia, serif; color: {{ colors.dark }}; font-size: 1.5rem; margin-top: 2.5rem; }
  .privacy ul { list-style: disc; padding-left: 1.25rem; }
  .privacy a { color: {{ colors.dark }}; font-weight: 500; text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 2px; }
  .privacy a:hover { color: {{ colors.accent }}; }
</style>

